ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS

The speculative parallel DEFLATE decompression algorithm in this project is
inspired by the pugz two-pass approach:

  pugz — Truly parallel gzip decompression
  Authors: Mael Kerbiriou, Rayan Chikhi
  License: MIT
  Repository: https://github.com/Piezoid/pugz
  Paper: "Parallel decompression of gzip-compressed files and random access
         to DNA sequences", HiCOMB 2019 (DOI: 10.1109/IPDPSW.2019.00042)

  The pugz algorithm uses speculative bit-level DEFLATE block boundary
  detection with a two-pass decode: pass 1 decodes all segments in parallel
  with empty windows (producing garbage in the first ≤32KB per segment),
  pass 2 sequentially fixes up each segment's beginning using the correct
  window from the previous segment's tail.

  lgz-rs implements a Rust adaptation of this concept using byte-aligned
  stored-block detection and miniz_oxide for the decode passes, optimized
  for modern multi-core CPUs with large caches and SIMD scanning.
